# Spring Boot Layering

Inbound transport (see also `10-java-hexagonal.mdc`):
- **`api`**: first-party public endpoints you own (today typically `api/rest`). Handle transport only (request parsing, edge validation, response mapping); delegate to `core/port/in`.
- **`adapters/in`**: external ingress (webhooks, third-party HTTP, external event consumers). Same rules—thin edge, then `core/port/in`; no domain orchestration here.

Application layer:
- orchestrate domain and output-port calls
- manage transactional flow intentionally
- avoid direct framework persistence objects in use-case signatures

Domain layer:
- preserve pure business invariants
- avoid framework coupling for business behavior

Infrastructure layer:
- implement adapters (persistence/integration/messaging)
- isolate framework clients and map to domain contracts

Spring conventions:
- prefer constructor injection
- keep configuration externalized
- centralize exception translation in shared handlers
- keep logging meaningful (operation, context, outcome)

## Testing — Security & AppAuthz in @WebMvcTest

PROHIBITED in test code:
- `spring.main.allow-bean-definition-overriding=true` — never use this property, not even in tests. It masks bean conflicts instead of resolving them.
- `@Bean("appAuthz")` overrides in `@TestConfiguration` — creates conflicts with the library-provided `AppAuthz` component.
- `@WithMockUser` on controller tests that use `@PreAuthorize("@appAuthz.isTenantMember(…)")` — produces `UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken` which `AppAuthz` cannot parse, always returning false.
- `@AutoConfigureMockMvc(addFilters = false)` to bypass security filters in security-related tests — defeats the purpose of testing authorization.

REQUIRED pattern (reference: `my-service` app):
- Use `@Import({AppAuthz.class, SecurityExceptionAdvice.class})` to load the real library beans.
- Build proper JWT authentication via a `AuthzTestJwtBuilder` test utility (per-app, in test sources). This builder uses `SecurityMockMvcRequestPostProcessors.jwt()` with YourApp claims (`app_authz_v`, `app_actor_type`, `app_client_type`, `app_tenants`, `tenants`).
- Apply JWT to requests: `.with(AuthzTestJwtBuilder.jwtMember(tenantId))` for authorized requests, `.with(AuthzTestJwtBuilder.jwtNonMember())` for denied requests.
- The real `AppAuthz.isTenantMember()` parses the JWT claims and evaluates tenant membership — no mocking or overriding needed.
